fbsdkpi: xnu memory pressure runs the Linux shrinkers and trims the page pool

One kernel thread per kext waits in mach_vm_pressure_monitor() (com.apple.kpi.mach) and, at
most once a second while the pageout daemon wants pages, calls linuxkpi's shrinkers
(pd_lkpi_lowmem(), the entry FreeBSD's vm_lowmem event would have used) and then returns
every free pool chunk to xnu (pd_linux_page_trim()). The seam half (pdos_pressure_start) is
in patch 0002's files, the pool half in 0011's.
UPSTREAM: yes.

--- a/src/Kernel/fbsdkpi/freebsd/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_shrinker.c
+++ b/src/Kernel/fbsdkpi/freebsd/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_shrinker.c
@@ -131,6 +131,14 @@
 	sx_xunlock(&sx_shrinker);
 }
 
+// PureDarwin: nothing raises FreeBSD's vm_lowmem event here; the page allocator's pressure
+// callback (pd_linux_page.c) calls this instead
+void
+pd_lkpi_lowmem(void)
+{
+	linuxkpi_vm_lowmem(NULL, 0);
+}
+
 static eventhandler_tag lowmem_tag;
 
 static void
